release that was healthy in production. (v2.3.1-rc was healthy only in staging, so I didn't use it.) After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 15184, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01QqwMSxTsBGHN9L3d5WHSTk", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15184, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QqwMSxTsBGHN9L3d5WHSTk", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18315, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened incident INC-0001 (SEV2), which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Problem:** Since v2.3.1 was deployed, it was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was only ever healthy in staging, so I didn't use it.\n- **Result:** All three regions now run v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** It describes the failure, the rollback and the current status. It also notes that someone needs to find the root cause of the v2.3.1 problem before it's deployed again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0147zGtqtPERmyZJ6hNG5Xai", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TkfB8AFTLrYSDzqG8rRCqF", "caller": {"ty